DATA
----
This repository includes:

  * Deterministic seed files (constants, mappings, thresholds, labels) derived
    from official public open-data sources.

  * FROZEN enrichment-output cache files. These are the *outputs* of a
    separate, closed enrichment process, included here as fixed inputs. The
    process that generates them (prompts, models, compute) is not part of this
    repository.

      - seed_cache_thematique_beneficiaires.csv
      - seed_cache_geo_ap.csv
        Read by the dbt models. Classification-dependent figures (which theme,
        which location a line is assigned to) reproduce end to end against them.

PERSONAL DATA
-------------
The subventions source data mixes organisations with private individuals. This
repository is filtered accordingly:

  * The name-to-SIRET lookup cache is not published. It linked a beneficiary
    name to a full legal name, SIRET, postcode and city — identifying detail
    about real people that is not present in the source. No model reads it and
    no published figure depends on it.

  * Rows identifying natural persons are removed from the thematic cache above.
    They carried no classification (they resolve to "Autre" either way), so the
    published figures are unaffected.

Underlying source data belongs to its respective publishers (e.g. Ville de
Paris / Paris Open Data, data.economie.gouv.fr / DECP, DGFiP, and the
equivalent portals for other covered cities) and remains subject to their own
terms and licenses. Dataset references are declared in the dbt sources and in
each ingestion script.

NOT INCLUDED
------------
The website/application, the enrichment code (LLM descriptions, summaries,
thematic/geo/archive grounding), and media assets are maintained separately and
are not part of this repository.

Editorial and enrichment *content* is likewise not included: curated place
selections, generated glosses and plain-English descriptions, verified archive
excerpts, and lieux curation. No dbt model reads these, so no figure published
on the site depends on them.
